<title>MEXICO: Abengoa wins contract for Mexico plants.</title>
<headline>Abengoa wins contract for Mexico plants.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Federal Electricity Commission (CFE) said on Thursday it awarded a contract to eight power substations to Spain's Abengoa, for a total of $34 million.</p>
<p>The construction will take place over the next two years, the CFE said, in the states of Tabasco, Campeche, Yucatan and Quintana Roo.</p>
<p>The projects are part of a total 15 contracts to build power stations being auctioned through September, for an expected investment of about $1.4 billion.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
